[# email/fallback-content: show one block in most clients and a simpler block in Outlook desktop.

   Uses conditional comments, which only Outlook desktop understands: `primary` is hidden from Outlook and
   `fallback` is shown only to it. Use it when a fancy block (a styled card, a stacked layout) degrades badly in
   the Word engine. Both slots take content-level components.

   Limits: conditional comments cannot be nested, so do not put components that emit their own (social-links,
   outlook-safe-button, button-group inline) in either slot. That is checked for raw markup you pass in.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: shows only `fallback`.
   - Gmail apps: shows only `primary`.
   - Dark mode: nothing extra, the components inside carry their own colors. #]
